{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1278828-what-s-your-opinion-on-the-jovian","id":1278828,"title":"What's your opinion on the Jovian?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-05T08:50:50-08:00","id":1278828,"title":"What's your opinion on the Jovian?","content":"I find it really really interesting, for many reason, especially its capability as a powerful plot device.<br /> <br /> Also, what origin would you like him to have? I'm torn between the qashmal and the god-machine ones","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My English sucks. Sorry.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23549-toreadorgentleman","name":"ToreadorGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T16:09:19-08:00","id":1278882,"title":"","content":"I think he serves as an excellent foil to the principle. the idea of continually dragging an agonizing existence in the guise of wisdom is interesting, along with how indirect the jovian is.<br /> <br /> as for origins, I do love the fallen qashmal one. to think that just one of these things losing it's way could lead to such a stagnating force","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T23:40:19-08:00","id":1278922,"title":"","content":"I tend to view <b>Promethean</b> as a sort of Christian allegory, a bit like the book <i>Pilgrim\u2019s Progress</i> \u2014 though not quite so blunt. In this view, the Principle takes the role of God, sending its <i>qashmal</i> agents to guide and test the Created on their Pilgrimage when It isn\u2019t guiding them \u201cdirectly\u201d through Elpis Visions. In this view, the Jovian takes on the role of the Devil, seeking to undermine the Principle\u2019s plans for the Created and to prevent them from completing their Pilgrimage. <br /> <br /> I generally view the Jovian as a fallen <i>archqashmal</i>; not the only one ever to have fallen, but the only one that has survived. It doesn\u2019t attempt to disrupt the Pilgrimage out of spite, at least not entirely. It does so out of self-interest: every Centimanus or Petrificatus feeds the Jovian by its mere existence; so the more Prometheans the Jovian can lead astray, the more powerful it becomes. <br /> <br /> If more than one Jovian exists, the power from the failed Prometheans gets split between them; so it has sought out and destroyed every other Jovian, sort of like a dark, morbid version of <i>Highlander</i>: there can be only one. This is also why it doesn\u2019t destroy Prometheans: it has nothing to gain by doing so if they stay on the Pilgrimage; plenty to gain if it can cause them to fail; and something to lose if they die after they have failed. There\u2019s no percentage in letting <i>any</i> Promethean perish. <br /> <br /> So how does a <i>qashmal</i> Fall? I don\u2019t know quite yet; but I\u2019m thinking that the Contagion might have something to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T05:23:48-08:00","id":1278946,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of not giving a concrete origin point. Giving rumours and hints at some greater story but leaving it fundamentally mysterious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T06:55:31-08:00","id":1278960,"title":"","content":"Surprisingly enough, the Jovian does not approve of Centimani (p. 159). It wants Prometheans to be stuck on the Pilgrimage, not to leave it altogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T16:38:58-08:00","id":1279072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1278828-what-s-your-opinion-on-the-jovian?p=1278960#post1278960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprisingly enough, the Jovian does not approve of Centimani (p. 159). It wants Prometheans to be stuck on the Pilgrimage, not to leave it altogether.</div> </div> </div> </div>was gonna say that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>. the Jovian will actively get rid of the hundred handed ones. it's important to note that the jovian is not an agent of flux (as in destruction). he is an agent of stagnation more than anything (its important to note that just like the archqashmal, the jovian does not represent creative or destructive force","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}